00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,000
[Six Months Ago]

2
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,000
You've been standing outside

3
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:44,080
for four minutes and 20 seconds.

4
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:45,920
How did you know?

5
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:47,600
I saw your shadow under the door.

6
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:27,600
Relax. There aren't any cameras here.

7
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,280
No security cameras downstairs either.

8
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:32,080
Every store on this street is run-down.

9
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,440
Relax. No one will know you were here.

10
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,080
My assistant knows.

11
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,680
I didn't tell him why I came up.

12
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,680
How do I know you won't tell anyone?

13
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:49,560
Hey, I ran into Hui Loek To on the street!

14
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,000
I even invited him over.

15
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:53,560
Are you crazy?

16
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,200
Why so nervous, To?

17
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,600
Your first time?

18
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,320
Are you done asking?

19
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,280
If you're uncomfortable,

20
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,880
you can leave anytime.

21
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,080
No one's keeping you here.

22
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,320
What, you think

23
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,760
anyone could keep me here?

24
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:45,880
I don't know.

25
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:47,680
Want to find out?

26
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:52,120
Any way I want?

27
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,400
How do you want to try?

28
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,120
You okay?

29
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,880
If you don't like it,

30
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:08,880
we can stop anytime.

31
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:12,720
Stop?

32
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:21,260
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

33
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:24,460
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

34
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:27,370
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

35
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,800
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

36
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:32,780
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

37
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:36,940
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

38
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,730
♪I'm willing to wait♪

39
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:45,420
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

40
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:48,220
♪I want to share my life with you♪

41
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:54,640
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

42
00:07:54,990 --> 00:07:56,790
♪In this cold and gray city♪

43
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:58,500
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

44
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,950
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

45
00:08:01,030 --> 00:08:01,610
♪Stay with me♪

46
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:04,360
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

47
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:05,140
♪Stay with me♪

48
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:08,060
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

49
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:10,560
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

50
00:08:11,090 --> 00:08:13,600
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

51
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:16,640
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

52
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:20,860
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

53
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,700
[Ash]
[Episode 2]

54
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,880
There are cops here.

55
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:31,000
- Cops!
- Police busted a drug deal last night.

56
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:34,320
Several suspected ringleaders were arrested.

57
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:38,840
- Police killed suspected dealers.
- Cops!

58
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:41,920
Another key member, known as Keung,

59
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,520
was shot and went missing at sea.

60
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:46,720
Police divers are searching for him.

61
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,300
[Kowloon East Crime Superintendent, Fung Hong Man]

62
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,720
[Death Confirmation Report]
Since Cheung Wai Keung is dead,

63
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:08,720
we'll close and archive the case.

64
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,280
I've got a new assignment for you.

65
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,720
Yes, sir! Thank you, sir!

66
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:16,520
Come in!

67
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:19,720
Hey, Officer Chan!

68
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,640
What's going on?

69
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,320
We just finished our briefing.

70
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,840
Already here to steal my guy? You're eager.

71
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:29,040
Of course.

72
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,720
I heard our rising star is finally free.

73
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:33,320
So I came right over to steal him from you.

74
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,520
Fei Foon, let me introduce you.

75
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:37,520
Officer Chan, Commercial Crime Bureau.

76
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:38,920
Good afternoon, sir!

77
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:39,920
Very polite.

78
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:44,200
Tall, handsome, and capable.

79
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:47,280
Quite the star. You've got a bright future.

80
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:48,320
Thank you, sir.

81
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,920
Just don't fall for me too quickly.

82
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:52,360
You haven't even seen my best qualities yet, sir.

83
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,920
That's a lot of confidence.

84
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:57,720
Confidence is a good thing.

85
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,720
Welcome to the Commercial Crime Bureau.

86
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:01,080
Can't wait to see what you can do.

87
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:02,520
Thank you, sir.

88
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,080
I won't let you down, Officer Chan.

89
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:07,280
Uh-oh. I think I'm falling for you already.

90
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,080
Hi, man.

91
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:16,720
Coming.

92
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,920
What are you taking pictures of?

93
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,720
You. I took some pictures of you sleeping.

94
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,160
Why are you taking pictures of me?

95
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,080
Am I not allowed to?

96
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:06,920
Let me see.

97
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,800
Fine, I'll show you.

98
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,200
Look how handsome you are.

99
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:15,040
Hey, don't take pictures of me in bed.

100
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,200
They're not bedroom pics.

101
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:20,920
Well?

102
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:22,160
Want to take one together?

103
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,080
I'll do it.

104
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,080
Why'd you bite me?

105
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,080
That's everything.

106
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:09,440
Thanks, man.

107
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,240
Hey, Dickson.

108
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,400
Long time no see.

109
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:27,280
Thought you ditched us after changing jobs.

110
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,920
I've just been busy lately.

111
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:29,720
I'd never ditch this place.

112
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:30,920
The usual.

113
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:32,320
Wait.

114
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,520
You got any smoky whiskey?

115
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,120
Come on, don't mess with me.

116
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:40,520
You think I carry fancy stuff like that?

117
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:41,720
Regular whiskey okay?

118
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:43,080
That'll do.

119
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:47,720
What's wrong?

120
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:50,040
You look like things aren't going your way.

121
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:51,800
I'm fine.

122
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,120
Work's been

123
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,920
going pretty well lately.

124
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,080
I'm not talking about work.

125
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,840
Guys only get this worked up over a few things.

126
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,080
Whiskey.

127
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,320
You don't miss a thing.

128
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,520
I brought this on myself.

129
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:09,040
I thought he was fun, so I made the first move.

130
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,720
Turns out I was the one who started it,

131
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,320
and I'm the one who fell for him.

132
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:18,520
I kept telling myself not to get attached.

133
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,400
Does he treat you well?

134
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,840
We usually get along pretty well.

135
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:26,200
No.

136
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:27,320
More like,

137
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,960
we get along when he's in a good mood.

138
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:34,600
The rest of the time, it's always his way.

139
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,520
He never asks what I want.

140
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,440
He's the worst.

141
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,400
It's actually pretty simple.

142
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:43,720
If you can't take it and you're miserable,

143
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:44,960
then leave.

144
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,320
Why stay with someone who doesn't care about you

145
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:49,120
and just keeps draining you? Right?

146
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,520
He's not worth it.

147
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:54,320
I thought I could just walk away too.

148
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,280
But it's not that simple.

149
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:57,920
True.

150
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,840
Otherwise, you wouldn't have come here alone

151
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:00,960
to drink with me, right?

152
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,920
Cheers.

153
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:04,440
Oh, shut up.

154
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,640
So, got any advice?

155
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:14,720
You're giving me the question of the century.

156
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,520
How about this?

157
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,160
Try something.

158
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,840
See if he actually cares about you.

159
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:23,280
If he does,

160
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,520
he'll change on his own.

161
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,520
If you test him and he doesn't react,

162
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:27,960
Break up with him.

163
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,080
Dump him.

164
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:32,520
Makes sense.

165
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:35,840
But sometimes I'm scared

166
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:39,080
I won't like the answer I get.

167
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:40,960
What's there to be scared of?

168
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:43,360
There's nothing a glass of whiskey can't fix.

169
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,800
And if that doesn't work,

170
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:46,720
have a few more.

171
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,600
Right?

172
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,080
Thanks.

173
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,280
Think it over.

174
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,280
Who are you?

175
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,280
Why are you following me?

176
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,440
Police. I'm going to search you.

177
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:26,440
Sir, please cooperate.

178
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:27,430
[Mok Fei Foon, Sergeant]

179
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,680
Forgot me already?

180
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:40,280
What are you playing at?

181
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:41,720
Messing with me?

182
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:43,280
To.

183
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:45,680
You know that's assaulting an officer.

184
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:47,520
You'd better be gentle.

185
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:04,320
That's all?

186
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:06,320
I was actually looking forward to it.

187
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:09,720
Keys.

188
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:11,440
Hand them over.

189
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:15,520
Can't find them.

190
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,920
Give me the keys. Now.

191
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,120
Haven't seen you in a while.

192
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,520
You're a lot bolder now.

193
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:01,120
When you first approached me,

194
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,920
was it because you were investigating me?

195
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,200
Is there something about you I should investigate?

196
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,720
You know Cheung Wai Keung is dead.

197
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:14,720
So?

198
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:17,920
So don't come looking for me at that place anymore.

199
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:23,720
Did I say I wanted to keep seeing you?

200
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:26,200
What?

201
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:28,320
Being a cop scares you?

202
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,360
Or do you only like guys like Cheung Wai Keung

203
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,520
because they're easier to control?

204
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,720
Say whatever you want.

205
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,720
Do you still want to keep this going?

206
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:52,280
No.

207
00:21:56,120 --> 00:21:57,120
Why?

208
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:03,040
Then what was that just now?

209
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,320
You came to me.

210
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:34,360
Come over. Let me introduce you.

211
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:36,320
I want you to meet our new guy.

212
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:37,080
Come on.

213
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:38,760
Mok Fei Foon.

214
00:22:38,920 --> 00:22:40,720
He's joining our Commercial Crime Bureau today.

215
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:42,440
Introduce yourself.

216
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:43,440
Hey, everyone.

217
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:44,560
Just call me Foon.

218
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,920
Let me introduce everyone.

219
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,520
Pang, Siu Kit, Ping, and On.

220
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:51,320
And this is Joseph.

221
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:52,720
He's new here too.

222
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:53,720
Nice to meet you, Officer Mok.

223
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:54,520
I'm Joseph.

224
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:55,720
If I ever mess something up

225
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:56,720
or do something wrong,

226
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:57,760
just tell me straight.

227
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:58,760
You can even chew me out.

228
00:22:58,840 --> 00:22:59,720
I'm always willing to learn.

229
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:02,560
No problem.

230
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:03,200
No need to be so formal.

231
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:04,560
We'll learn from each other.

232
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,200
Alright.

233
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:07,520
He's fresh out of the academy

234
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:08,280
and still pretty green.

235
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:09,720
Keep an eye on him for me.

236
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:10,720
Okay?

237
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:12,320
Now that everyone's met,

238
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,560
let's get to work.

239
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:19,040
Looks like a big case.

240
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:20,280
Yeah.

241
00:23:20,320 --> 00:23:22,120
You got a big one on your first day.

242
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:24,320
According to Interpol,

243
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:26,960
for the past year, a group called Dreamweaver has been running

244
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:28,560
a global counterfeiting ring, producing fake currencies worldwide

245
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:31,200
[Counterfeit Currencies: HKD, MOP]
with alarming aggressiveness.

246
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:35,440
[Japanese Yen]
Worth tens of billions of dollars.

247
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,320
Their crimes

248
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,960
span Europe, the Americas, and even Asia.

249
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:41,560
According to our intel,

250
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:43,280
they may already be in Hong Kong, China.

251
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:51,920
These are really well made.

252
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:54,720
Even I can't tell they're fake.

253
00:23:55,360 --> 00:23:56,560
It's not just you.

254
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,080
Even counterfeit detectors can't spot them.

255
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:08,280
I've had several banks test them.

256
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:09,320
Only the latest

257
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:10,720
counterfeit detectors can spot

258
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:11,760
the difference.

259
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:13,960
But most places don't have equipment that advanced.

260
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:14,720
Right?

261
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:17,680
We've had several reports recently.

262
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,760
Banks across Hong Kong, China

263
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:22,040
have been receiving these new counterfeit bills.

264
00:24:22,520 --> 00:24:24,120
But according to our intel,

265
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,680
there are two major channels for counterfeit money here.

266
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:30,280
[Operation Gutenberg]
First is the old Eastern Hall gang.

267
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:33,120
Their main business in Southeast Asia

268
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,200
is arms trafficking.

269
00:24:34,760 --> 00:24:36,920
[Ho Tung Fong]
They found out during an earlier deal

270
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:38,320
they'd paid with counterfeit bills.

271
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:39,680
And it was a large amount.

272
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:42,680
So they likely got the bills from Dreamweaver.

273
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:44,920
The second channel

274
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:47,440
is Sheng Tung's uncle,

275
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:49,120
To Si Hong.

276
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:50,090
[To Si Hong]

277
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:51,520
According to overseas intel,

278
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:54,120
he's used counterfeit bills at several casinos.

279
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,560
He's been identified and blacklisted for a while.

280
00:24:56,760 --> 00:24:58,720
To Si Hong is currently in Hong Kong, China.

281
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:00,720
We plan to start with him.

282
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:03,520
Foon, you're taking this lead.

283
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:04,560
Understood, sir.

284
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:06,200
Officer Mok needs a partner too.

285
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:07,920
Can I go with him?

286
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:10,720
Alright.

287
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:13,360
You'll learn a lot working with a veteran.

288
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,520
Everyone, move fast.

289
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:16,320
Make sure you note the key details.

290
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:18,560
We'll meet with Interpol online shortly

291
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:19,680
to get the latest on their investigation.

292
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:20,960
If they make any move,

293
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:22,200
we'll give them our full support.

294
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:24,720
We have to catch the mastermind behind Dreamweaver.

295
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:25,560
Clear?

296
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:26,280
Yes, sir!

297
00:25:27,040 --> 00:25:28,280
I'll go get things ready for the meeting.

298
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:31,720
Officer Mok, I look forward to learning from you.

299
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,680
If I mess up, just set me straight.

300
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:35,280
No problem.

301
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:36,320
Good.

302
00:25:39,100 --> 00:25:41,460
[Golden Dream Nightclub]

303
00:25:41,460 --> 00:25:44,070
[Golden Treasure Karaoke Nightclub]

304
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:51,780
[Harbour Crystal Centre]

305
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:07,720
I told you to wash the car, not stare at it.

306
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:11,200
Look busy doing your own thing

307
00:26:11,480 --> 00:26:13,560
while keeping a close eye on the target.

308
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:14,920
Got it?

309
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:17,200
Sorry. I'm a little nervous.

310
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,120
Don't apologize to me.

311
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:20,120
If this goes sideways,

312
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:21,120
you're taking the fall.

313
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:21,960
What?

314
00:26:22,520 --> 00:26:23,960
Don't "what" me. Keep washing.

315
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,280
Officer Mok.

316
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:36,760
That's a nice lighter.

317
00:26:36,840 --> 00:26:37,720
Where'd you get it?

318
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:38,960
We're working.

319
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:41,200
Stay focused. No irrelevant questions.

320
00:26:43,760 --> 00:26:45,800
What do you think To Si Hong is doing here?

321
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:48,200
Based on the intel,

322
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:50,520
this is probably an illegal casino.

323
00:26:50,760 --> 00:26:52,800
No surprise he'd come here to scam some money.

324
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:54,280
Officer Mok.

325
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:55,920
You really know your stuff. That's impressive.

326
00:26:56,360 --> 00:26:57,600
This is basic stuff.

327
00:26:58,200 --> 00:26:59,560
You should've learned plenty at the academy.

328
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:03,560
My academy instructors weren't as good as you.

329
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:04,960
They couldn't teach real field experience.

330
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,960
You can't say that.

331
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:10,320
Most of what your instructors teach you

332
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:11,560
is how to stay alive.

333
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:13,680
Apologize to them right now.

334
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:14,680
Now?

335
00:27:14,720 --> 00:27:15,320
Right now.

336
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:16,960
Apologize while you wash the car.

337
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,200
Pick up the pace.

338
00:27:19,280 --> 00:27:20,720
Or I'm leaving you here after the shift.

339
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:21,960
Okay.

340
00:27:22,200 --> 00:27:23,200
Sorry, sir.

341
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:24,960
Sorry, sir.

342
00:27:25,360 --> 00:27:27,560
Sorry, sir.

343
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:37,440
They're not even trying out there.

344
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:40,320
Exactly. They can barely stay on their feet.

345
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:43,840
What are they doing? Still no goal!

346
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:46,200
Next bet's on the home team to score. Go!

347
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,680
Hurry up!

348
00:27:57,320 --> 00:27:58,120
Place the bet.

349
00:27:58,440 --> 00:27:59,280
50,000.

350
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:19,920
Vincent.

351
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:21,680
Vincent, let me explain.

352
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:22,720
Just hear me out.

353
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:23,760
Please, let me explain first.

354
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:28,840
Uncle To.

355
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:31,920
I let it slide when you were making money on the side.

356
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,560
I didn't hold it against you.

357
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:37,200
But you scammed money from our own operation.

358
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:40,200
I know I messed up!

359
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:41,440
I just wasn't thinking straight!

360
00:28:41,840 --> 00:28:43,200
It was a stupid mistake!

361
00:28:44,360 --> 00:28:45,320
How much is left?

362
00:28:45,760 --> 00:28:46,520
I spent it all.

363
00:28:46,760 --> 00:28:48,040
Nothing's left. Not a cent.

364
00:28:53,040 --> 00:28:54,440
Don't lie to me!

365
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:55,920
Where'd you get those counterfeit bills?

366
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:57,680
Well...

367
00:28:57,760 --> 00:28:59,080
A contact hooked me up

368
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:00,440
with a friend who supplied them.

369
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,960
You just borrowed money from the gang

370
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:04,040
because you said you were short on cash.

371
00:29:04,080 --> 00:29:05,720
So where'd you get that much money?

372
00:29:11,760 --> 00:29:13,120
Talk!

373
00:29:16,920 --> 00:29:18,320
I know I messed up.

374
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:20,720
I got greedy.

375
00:29:20,760 --> 00:29:21,560
I'm sorry.

376
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:22,920
I know you messed up.

377
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:25,200
The gang left

378
00:29:25,200 --> 00:29:26,280
over three million with you.

379
00:29:26,520 --> 00:29:27,920
Is that money still there?

380
00:29:29,040 --> 00:29:30,440
I'm sorry.

381
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:32,320
I'm sorry.

382
00:29:32,360 --> 00:29:33,520
I won't do it again.

383
00:29:33,520 --> 00:29:34,440
Never again.

384
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:35,280
Uncle To.

385
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:37,520
You've been with Sheng Tung for years.

386
00:29:37,520 --> 00:29:39,040
You know the rules.

387
00:29:39,120 --> 00:29:41,600
The rules? No!

388
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:45,720
Vincent, no!

389
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:47,520
Fung, no!

390
00:29:47,720 --> 00:29:48,720
Vincent!

391
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:54,800
No!

392
00:29:57,560 --> 00:29:59,040
Take him to Dr. Chan.

393
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:00,920
Wait!

394
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:23,360
Find out who he's been in contact with lately.

395
00:30:24,080 --> 00:30:26,680
You don't usually go this far.

396
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:28,920
Why are you so worked up?

397
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:32,600
Guys like him don't matter if they die.

398
00:30:33,520 --> 00:30:34,280
Then

399
00:30:34,840 --> 00:30:36,520
whose death would matter?

400
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:47,920
Two guys outside are acting suspicious.

401
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:49,360
Want me to check them out?

402
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:56,200
Tell the guys outside to stay sharp, just in case.

403
00:30:57,280 --> 00:30:58,040
And...

404
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:00,720
Find out what those two are investigating.

405
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:03,520
If you're worried about him, just call him.

406
00:31:04,120 --> 00:31:05,120
Why do you always make me check on him?

407
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,520
I call you all the time too.

408
00:31:06,840 --> 00:31:08,520
Does that mean I'm worried about you?

409
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:10,920
I already know you care about me.

410
00:31:11,600 --> 00:31:13,440
Always working late, keeping me by your side.

411
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:15,040
But we can never be together.

412
00:31:15,680 --> 00:31:16,680
Just let me go.

413
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:19,960
Go.

414
00:31:20,760 --> 00:31:21,760
You talk too much.

415
00:31:23,600 --> 00:31:24,360
Sorry, sir.

416
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:27,440
Sorry, sir.

417
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:29,440
Sorry, sir.

418
00:31:42,360 --> 00:31:43,440
Careful!

419
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:52,440
Officer Mok, are you okay?

420
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:53,280
I'm fine.

421
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:56,040
Run XW2927.

422
00:31:56,560 --> 00:31:58,520
What's XW2927?

423
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:02,280
The license plate!

424
00:32:03,600 --> 00:32:05,360
You really worry me sometimes.

425
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:07,920
Officer Mok, you're bleeding.

426
00:32:07,920 --> 00:32:09,080
Want me to bandage it?

427
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:12,520
Help me back so you can bandage me.

428
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:14,440
And maybe get your head checked while we're at it.

429
00:32:15,480 --> 00:32:16,680
Careful.

430
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:17,960
Careful.

431
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:18,720
Careful.

432
00:32:18,760 --> 00:32:19,200
I'm fine.

433
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:19,840
Go.

434
00:32:19,960 --> 00:32:20,960
Careful.

435
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:22,200
Careful. Hold on.

436
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:24,200
Careful. Hold on.

437
00:32:29,760 --> 00:32:30,680
Alright.

438
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:33,960
- Careful. - I know.

439
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:44,720
Why is this taking so long?

440
00:32:45,080 --> 00:32:46,520
I'm afraid I'll hurt you.

441
00:32:47,160 --> 00:32:48,520
All done. Let's get back to work.

442
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,760
Officer Mok, don't you need to rest?

443
00:32:51,880 --> 00:32:53,040
Don't you have work to do?

444
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:55,040
Did you finish the report?

445
00:32:55,520 --> 00:32:56,960
Did you run the plate?

446
00:32:57,560 --> 00:32:59,360
Or were you planning to let AI do it for you?

447
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:01,600
I'll finish it in a bit.

448
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:06,200
Officer Mok, you're leaving?

449
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:08,440
We're done for today.

450
00:33:08,840 --> 00:33:10,280
Why don't I drive you home?

451
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:11,920
You did just get hurt.

452
00:33:15,480 --> 00:33:17,200
What? Is there something on my face?

453
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:18,920
Sometimes I really wonder

454
00:33:19,560 --> 00:33:21,520
if you actually want to be a cop.

455
00:33:21,920 --> 00:33:23,680
Your work isn't done and you're ready to leave.

456
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:25,360
But you...

457
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:28,920
Don't worry about me.

458
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:32,720
It's just my hand. I won't die.

459
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:34,520
Stop hovering over me.

460
00:33:34,920 --> 00:33:36,680
Finish up and go home early.

461
00:33:37,520 --> 00:33:38,320
See you tomorrow.

462
00:33:50,960 --> 00:33:51,720
Seriously?

463
00:34:00,520 --> 00:34:01,560
What are you doing here?

464
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:03,280
Were you following me?

465
00:34:03,280 --> 00:34:04,040
Yeah.

466
00:34:04,200 --> 00:34:05,560
You've been messing with me this whole time.

467
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:07,520
You think I'm just going to let that slide?

468
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:08,120
You...

469
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:14,520
I've slept less than six hours total these past few days.

470
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:15,840
I'm not in the mood for your games.

471
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:17,760
Give me back my key.

472
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:29,360
Why are you still standing there?

473
00:34:29,720 --> 00:34:30,960
Waiting to see when you'd go home.

474
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:33,520
Whether I go home is none of your business.

475
00:34:35,720 --> 00:34:36,920
You look exhausted.

476
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:37,720
I wanted to keep you company.

477
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:41,960
I can handle things myself.

478
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:43,120
You don't need to worry about me.

479
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:44,600
I know you can handle it alone.

480
00:34:46,560 --> 00:34:47,360
But...

481
00:34:48,720 --> 00:34:50,360
You don't have to.

482
00:35:11,560 --> 00:35:12,680
Where's the bathroom?

483
00:35:18,160 --> 00:35:18,920
This way.

484
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:21,720
Take a shower. Get in.

485
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:24,520
Mr. Hui, I told you.

486
00:35:24,560 --> 00:35:26,280
I'm exhausted today.

487
00:35:26,720 --> 00:35:28,760
That's not what I meant.

488
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:41,160
Get in.

489
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:44,720
You want me in the tub with my clothes on?

490
00:35:45,360 --> 00:35:46,960
I said get in, so get in.

491
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,680
Hey! Knock it off!

492
00:36:18,280 --> 00:36:19,400
Are you crazy?

493
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:27,960
Awake now?

494
00:36:29,480 --> 00:36:30,760
Are you seeing someone else?

495
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:33,360
What are you talking about?

496
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:35,840
Some guy's been with you all day,

497
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:37,520
getting all cozy with you.

498
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:39,040
I haven't seen you for a few days,

499
00:36:40,280 --> 00:36:41,840
and you've already hooked him?

500
00:36:42,520 --> 00:36:44,040
So what if I have?

501
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:45,360
None of your business!

502
00:36:47,560 --> 00:36:48,840
So you'll sleep with just anyone.

503
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:51,360
Who I'm with

504
00:36:51,440 --> 00:36:52,440
and what we do

505
00:36:52,720 --> 00:36:54,360
is none of your business.

506
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:56,040
Get out. Now!

507
00:36:56,440 --> 00:36:57,640
Don't make a mess of my place.

508
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:04,760
I'm the only one you're allowed to have.

509
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:09,440
You and I are over.

510
00:37:10,560 --> 00:37:11,760
We don't have to be.

511
00:37:12,080 --> 00:37:13,360
But you can't see anyone else.

512
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:14,760
What did you say?

513
00:37:15,560 --> 00:37:17,360
You wanted to keep going in that alley, right?

514
00:37:18,360 --> 00:37:19,280
Now I'm saying yes.

515
00:37:19,360 --> 00:37:20,360
Do you have two personalities or something?

516
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:21,400
You change your mind every five minutes.

517
00:37:21,520 --> 00:37:22,520
"Yes" or

518
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:23,720
"No"?

519
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:24,920
Don't waste my time.

520
00:37:26,440 --> 00:37:27,360
Well...

521
00:37:28,560 --> 00:37:29,680
No.

522
00:37:30,200 --> 00:37:30,960
Why?

523
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:32,840
You think I'm stupid?

524
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:35,640
First you said I threw myself at you.

525
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:38,600
Then today you soaked me.

526
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:40,160
You think I'd take you back?

527
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,840
So you don't want to keep this going?

528
00:37:43,040 --> 00:37:43,640
Right.

529
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:47,040
You want me to leave right now?

530
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:47,680
Right.

531
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:50,360
You said it.

532
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:25,520
What are you trying to do now?

533
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:28,360
I'll help you undress.

534
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:31,400
Keep this nonsense up,

535
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:33,440
and I'll charge you with trespassing!

536
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:34,160
Fine.

537
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:40,520
Take it off.

538
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:53,520
Sit down.

539
00:38:59,200 --> 00:39:00,680
Sit. I'll wash your hair.

540
00:39:08,720 --> 00:39:09,760
To.

541
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,840
Look at you. Not bad at all.

542
00:39:15,600 --> 00:39:17,280
When my little brother was a kid,

543
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:19,640
I used to bathe him.

544
00:39:30,440 --> 00:39:31,160
Did your wound heal?

545
00:39:32,480 --> 00:39:33,280
What?

546
00:39:38,040 --> 00:39:38,720
Here.

547
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:41,960
You got hit with an ashtray.

548
00:39:44,160 --> 00:39:45,400
It's nothing.

549
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:47,400
My hair usually covers it,

550
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:48,440
so you can't tell.

551
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:52,360
I'm sorry.

552
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:57,840
Why the long face?

553
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:01,960
I won't let anything like that happen again.

554
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:35,280
What's this supposed to mean?

555
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:37,280
You said your counterfeit bills were top quality!

556
00:40:37,680 --> 00:40:38,720
So how did they get spotted?

557
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:41,200
How much did you use at once?

558
00:40:41,520 --> 00:40:42,520
Yeah.

559
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:44,280
I used them in large batches.

560
00:40:44,440 --> 00:40:46,120
Your bills are the problem here.

561
00:40:46,520 --> 00:40:47,720
If your product was good enough,

562
00:40:48,080 --> 00:40:49,160
it wouldn't matter how much I used!

563
00:40:49,560 --> 00:40:50,600
No matter how good the craftsmanship is,

564
00:40:50,760 --> 00:40:52,120
counterfeit money is still counterfeit.

565
00:40:52,680 --> 00:40:53,840
Using a large amount at once

566
00:40:54,200 --> 00:40:55,040
is bound to raise suspicion.

